{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1381656-thoughts-on-this-origins-antagonist-the-temple-killer","id":1381656,"title":"Thoughts on this Origins antagonist: The Temple Killer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T08:57:45-07:00","id":1381656,"title":"Thoughts on this Origins antagonist: The Temple Killer","content":"While thinking up up possible foes for a Scion Origins Chronicle i might run one day i thought up an interesting one i want some feedback on. My idea so far is a unassuming, mousy, George Mcfly-like accountant named Herbert Dawson. He works as an accountant for a multi-national firm and is a generally unassuming man, but is actually harboring a dark and sinister secret. My idea so far is that he is a serial killer whose M.O involves luring &quot;wicked men&quot; into temples or sacred sites of various justice, vengeance, war, or other seemingly &quot;violent&quot; gods of the various Pantheons and horrifically murdering them in a way that makes it look like the god themselves murdered the &quot;sinner&quot;, bringing them to justice. If there is a statue, he often decorates it with the blood, and sometimes a body part or two of his victims, as if the statue itself came to life and did the bloody work<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> His motivation involves him having his family murdered by a criminal with tight ties to the city he lives in. The criminal, of course, was arrested and Herbert, despite not being a very spiritual man, prayed to the various pantheons, promising much in exchange for justice being delivered to this seemingly untouchable killer. But, his prayers went unanswered and the killer went free. This made Hubert furious and he began seeking vengeance, even calling down the Furies on the criminal. But, when nothing still happened, he finally stopped, realizing that if the God's wouldn't grant his vengeance, he would himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am debating between two reasons for choosing temples and sacred sites. One idea I had was that he still trying to have vengeance on the very same criminal who murdered his family, but has no way to find him. So, he is offering up his victims as sacrifices to these various gods, in hopes that one notices him and either grants his vengeance or at least gives him the power to do so himself. My other idea is that he is furious with the God's and their &quot;neglect&quot;, so he has decided to fulfill his murderous fantasies in their own sacred sites, mimicking the God's as a attempt to disrespect them and their temples. Can i have your thoughts on this antagonist and how to make him a threat to pre-visitation Scions and how to make it work in the Scion universe? Which motive seems more plausible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:33:46-07:00","id":1381694,"title":"","content":"Honestly, at Origin tier, A Dedicated Guy With A Knife can be a sufficient threat for your players, if he's clever.<br /> <br /> I rather like the motif you're going for. You can make him a particularly driven otherwise normal person. Or if you want to be spicy, maybe consider making him a Sorcerer whose offerings are a way to fuel his awakening powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T06:49:45-07:00","id":1382145,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Will have to think about those two options. One part i gotta plan out is the murders the PCs stumble upon. I already got some ideas for a Kali themed murder and for some of the Aztec Gods. But, i wonder what murders themed off of Bast and one of the Shinto gods would be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 04-17-2020, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T10:56:57-07:00","id":1382199,"title":"","content":"Now be careful with those, as Kali and the Teotl have in the past had some unsavory images slapped on them.<br /> <br /> Maybe have priests of these Gods make background statements disavowing any connection to the murders. And maybe learn a bit about proper rites and rituals so that when your High Culture or Occult characters case the scene, you can go &quot;You would know that a ritual to Huitzilopochtli wouldn't look like this because X, Y, and Z&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}